  // Support
  support_title: 'Support',
  support_subtitle: 'QNet Wallet on phones and tablets, and the browser extension',
  support_contact_title: 'Contact',
  support_contact_email: 'Email: {address}',
  support_contact_bugs: 'Bugs and feature requests: {link}',
  support_contact_bugs_link: 'GitHub issues',
  support_contact_community: 'Community: {link}',
  support_contact_docs: 'Documentation: {link}',
  support_never_share: 'Never send your recovery phrase or private key to anyone, including anyone claiming to be support. Nobody who works on QNet Blockchain will ever ask for it, and nobody can restore a wallet without it.',
  support_lost_title: 'I lost my recovery phrase',
  support_lost: 'There is no recovery. The wallet is non-custodial: the recovery phrase exists only where you wrote it down. If it is gone, the wallet cannot be restored on a new device. While you still have access to the wallet, open Settings, show the phrase and write it down; keep it offline.',
  support_pending_title: 'My transaction shows "Awaiting confirmation" or "Pending"',
  support_pending_lead: 'QNet Blockchain has not confirmed it yet, so the outcome is not known. The wallet keeps asking the chain and updates the history when it knows. Sending the same payment again can pay it twice:',
  support_pending_app: 'In the mobile app, the next send from that wallet asks what to do with the unconfirmed one. Replace it: the new send takes its place, and only one of the two can go through. Send in addition: both can go through.',
  support_pending_extension: 'In the browser extension, the send review lists the unconfirmed transfers and offers to replace one of them (only one of the two can go through); otherwise the new send goes in addition, and all of them can go through.',
  support_pending_once: 'To be charged once, wait until the first transaction is confirmed, or open the address in the explorer and check it, before you send the payment again.',
  support_epochs_title: 'My light node misses epochs',
  support_epochs_lead: 'A light node answers the status requests of QNet Blockchain while QNet Wallet runs on its device: open, in the background or behind the lock screen. What can delay or skip its answers:',
  support_epochs_closed: 'Closing the app from the list of recent apps, or a force stop: the node then does not answer until the app is opened again.',
  support_epochs_battery: 'Battery restrictions for the app: allow QNet Wallet to run in the background in the device\'s settings. A battery-saving mode can also hold background answers back while it is on.',
  support_epochs_offline: 'The device has to be online at least sometimes. With no connection for a whole four-hour epoch there is nothing to answer the epoch with.',
  support_epochs_apple: 'iPhone and iPad: Background App Refresh has to be on. In Settings, then General, then Background App Refresh, it must not be Off, and the switch next to QNet Wallet must be on. Without it, and in Low Power Mode, which turns it off, the node answers only while the app is open.',
  support_epochs_android: 'Android: the usual battery setting is enough on most phones. If the Node tab counts fewer epochs than have passed while the phone was online, open Settings, then Apps, then QNet Wallet, and set its battery use to Unrestricted (on some phones: No restrictions). Some phones also need the app allowed to start by itself.',
  support_epochs_sleep: 'An ordinary sleeping device is not a problem: QNet Blockchain repeats its requests during the epoch, and any answer counts that comes before the epoch\'s check closes, about 2.5 minutes before the epoch ends. An answer after that counts for no epoch, not the next one either.',
  support_device_title: 'The node does not run on this device',
  support_device_lead: 'A light node runs on one phone or tablet at a time. If the Node tab says that the node is paused on this device, or that this device can\'t run a node, run it on another phone or tablet: install QNet Wallet there from the app store, open this wallet with its recovery phrase and link the node to that device. The wallet and the node balance are not affected, and the balance can still be moved into the wallet ({rules}).',
  support_device_rules_link: 'Device rules',
  support_move_title: 'The old Android app asks me to install the new QNet Wallet',
  support_move: 'An earlier Android build of QNet Wallet installed from a file is a separate, older app, and its last update asks you to move. Install QNet Wallet from Google Play or from the {walletPage}: it is the same app. Restore the wallet in it with the recovery phrase — the funds are on the chain, not in the app — and remove the old app once the new one shows the wallet. To run the wallet\'s light node in the new app, link the new device on My node (Device tab) and confirm in QNet Wallet.',
  support_move_wallet_link: 'wallet page',
  support_history_title: 'Where is my history',
  support_history: 'The wallet shows history from the aiqnet.io explorer archive together with the freshest data from the nodes. A row opens the transaction in the explorer; a pending row copies its hash instead. If a transfer is missing, open the address in the {explorer} — the chain is the record.',
  support_history_explorer_link: 'explorer',
  support_legal_title: 'Legal',
