  home_phase: 'Phase {n}',
  home_phase1_title: '1DEV burn',
  home_phase1_body: '1DEV tokens are burned on Solana for node activation: 1,500 1DEV for any node type, and the amount decreases as the supply burns. The tokens are destroyed and nobody receives them. The nodes of QNet Blockchain verify the burn transaction themselves: no bridge and no wrapped assets.',
  home_phase2_title: 'QNC to Pool #3',
  home_phase2_when: 'Starts when 90% of the original 1DEV supply is burned or five years after the genesis block, whichever comes first.',
  home_phase2_body: 'Activation spends QNC, which goes to Pool #3 and is redistributed to all active nodes. The amount scales with network size; the exact schedule is set before Phase 2 opens.',
  home_halving_title: 'Sharp drop halving',
  home_halving_label: 'Base emission by year on a log scale: halved every 4 years to year 20, divided by 10 for years 20 to 24, then halved every 4 years again',
  home_halving_unit: 'base emission, log scale',
  home_halving_years: 'years',
  home_halving_caption: 'Years 0–20: ÷2 every 4 years. Years 20–24: a sharp drop, ÷10. From year 24, halving resumes from the low base.',
  home_mult_title: 'Activation amount by network size',
  home_mult_1: '0–100,000 nodes',
  home_mult_2: '100,000–300,000 nodes',
  home_mult_3: '300,000–1,000,000 nodes',
  home_mult_4: '1,000,000+ nodes',
  home_mult_caption: 'Multiplier on the Phase 2 activation amount. Every Phase 2 activation goes to Pool #3.',
  home_pools_title: 'Two reward pools',
  home_pools_1: 'Base emission on the halving schedule, split each epoch among the nodes recorded as online.',
  home_pools_2: 'Pool #3, fed by Phase 2 activations and shared by all active nodes.',
  home_pools_fees: 'Transaction fees go to the block producer.',
  home_security_title: 'Security model',
  home_pq_title: 'Post-quantum cryptography',
  home_pq_body: 'Signatures are ML-DSA-65 (NIST FIPS 204) only, on every transaction and consensus message, for wallets, nodes and consensus alike. Nodes talk over TLS 1.3 on QUIC with a hybrid X25519 + ML-KEM-768 (FIPS 203) key exchange, authenticated with ML-DSA-65.',
  home_rep_datum: 'Equal nodes, proven faults',
  home_rep_title: 'Reputation-based security',
  home_rep_body: 'No token locking, no slashing of funds. Producers and committees are drawn by verifiable randomness from all eligible nodes. A node that signs two conflicting blocks is proven on chain and removed from every future draw; everyone else keeps full liquidity and an equal say.',
  home_rate_datum: 'Per-IP limits',
  home_rate_title: 'Rate limiting',
  home_rate_body: 'Each node\'s public API limits every IP address (an IPv6 address by its /64): 100 transaction submissions and 300 reads a minute, and 5 activations an hour, with a pause after a limit is passed. Incoming transactions are checked in a separate, bounded verification pool, and block validation keeps a pool of its own.',
  home_mobile_title: 'Mobile-first blockchain',
  home_mobile_lead: 'A blockchain designed for phones: participation is a signed answer, not proof-of-work',
  home_presence_title: 'Presence, not proof-of-work',
  home_presence_body: 'A light node answers a signed status request from QNet Blockchain a few times per four-hour epoch. Between requests the app only sends one signed attestation per epoch. No hashing and no proof-of-work: each answer is one signature, so the phone does no sustained work.',
  home_app_title: 'One app on every phone and tablet',
  home_app_body: 'The same app and the same screens on iPhone, iPad and Android phones and tablets: silent push wake-ups for status requests, and an unlock with Face ID, Touch ID, a fingerprint or the device passcode, or an app password on a device without them.',
  home_app_stores: 'On {play} now; on iPhone and iPad on the {appStore}.',
  home_app_stores_testflight: 'On {play} now; on iPhone and iPad from {testflight} until the App Store listing is live.',
  home_app_languages: 'In 11 languages:',
  home_hw_title: 'Hardware-backed security',
  home_hw_body: 'Post-quantum keys are encrypted at rest and protected by the system keystore. A light node is bound to one device by a key in its secure hardware: one device runs one node, and computers and emulators run none.',
  home_split_title: 'How emission is split',
  home_split_body: 'For each epoch QNet Blockchain records which nodes were online. The protocol adds a share of that epoch\'s emission to their node balance (three quarters among light nodes, one quarter among super nodes), and the wallet moves it into itself with an ordinary transaction.',
  home_split_label: 'Three quarters of each epoch\'s emission to light nodes, one quarter to super nodes',
